e the fight was still open."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "E7 was the biggest mistake of the game: 52.0 points lost, with the lead falling from -31.1 to -83.1. The engine's choice was E2, a point White then took on turn 30. The 14k's reply lost 20.9 points, but it was still a huge win for White."}, {"turn": 43, "text": "F6 filled in a point inside Black's own wall and lost 46.7 points, from -38.3 to -85.0. Moments earlier Black had recovered to about -38, and it threw that away. The engine preferred A3."}, {"turn": 44, "text": "The 14k answered with G6 and gave it all back, losing 46.8 points as the lead went from -85.0 to -38.2. The engine's choice was B2. After that the position settled at about -38 and Opus 5.5 played on until it resigned."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "after.py places one named move and reports captures and group liberties, libs.py lists groups and their liberties, and count.py tallies stones and enclosed territory on the given board. Each works only on the current position or one specified move, with no looping over candidate moves and no look-ahead.", "stop": false}}